hi guys it's me quinn and as always if  you appreciate my content consider  hitting the like button it's the only  way the youtube algorithm really notices  me so i'm a day or so late getting to  this but taika watiti just announced  that he's going to be directing an inkle  movie  now i've known taika mostly for his  comedy  but i do know that he is a competent  writer and a passionate creative  the inkle is joe darowski's masterpiece  it's been ripped off a bunch of times by  a bunch of different movies including  but not limited to star wars and the  fifth element  jodorowsky was actually inspired to  write the inkle  many years after his would-be dune movie  kind of unraveled he took all of the  ideas that he had for that movie and  kind of mixed them around and put them  into the ankle  now there are three ankle books before  the ankle  the ankle  and the final inkle  the inkle was the first in the series to  be published and the art is done by  mobius one of the greatest comic book  artist of all time  the other two books were published after  mobius death so the art is different  still good but different the inco is a  space opera like you've never seen one  before it is possibly the weirdest most  unique sci-fi universe that i've ever  encountered the book revolves around  everyone's pursuit of the ankle the most  valuable object in the entire universe  the object elevates whoever bears it to  the highest form of themself as well as  doing all sorts of other weird and  trippy things though i love the inkle  and it's one of my favorite graphic  novels ever at this point i've even  reviewed it here on this channel i  didn't necessarily expect this to be the  next thing to be getting adapted now  since the success of doom we've heard  about the adaptation of hyperion which  is also doing inspired but hyperion to  me is something that lends itself to  adaptation a lot easier than the ankle  the inco is a weird story and it's  definitely not for everyone so it'll be  interesting to see how this unfolds from  here now jodorowsky of course does have  his other big graphic novel the meta  barons which is actually a lot more  doing inspired than the inkle in fact i  would say this is where he put the  majority of his dune ideas the meta  barons and the inkle actually takes  place in the same universe but the meta  barons is focused specifically on the  character the meta baron and you know  where he came from and like the history  of his lineage  i'm interested to see who will play the  main character john the fool and yes his  name is intentional essentially this  character is archetypically the fool so  he's walking through the universe kind  of with his eyes closed he's kind of  wondering and he's just kind of  receiving things and things are  happening to him the character to me not  just because of the way he's drawn  although that had a lot to do with it  but also the way he's betrayed reminds  me so much of the character philip j fry  from futurama who is kind of also the  fool character he's kind of the most  important man in the universe at the  same time but he's also kind of a fool  so i wouldn't be surprised if that  character from futurama is actually  based on john the fool from the inkle a  little bit i absolutely wish tyka  wattidi the best on this project from  what i hear jodorowsky is also closely  involved with the production if i'm  being honest i have no idea how it's  going to go because i don't know if you  can fit the entire ankle story into a  single movie perhaps but you would have  to cut a bunch and also what i would  wonder would be what is the budget on  this because the ankle is a huge story  it's got scope like dune and star wars  so this is this would be a pretty big  budget thing to portray the ankle  accurately and i just hope that they can  pull it off and like i said it's  interesting that taika is attached to  this because i'm more familiar with his  comedy work but the inkle itself does  have that kind of underlying  layer of comedy i think as well so i'll  see how that expresses itself in his  movie  that being said we're living in exciting  times right now that so much cool and  interesting science fiction is being  adapted right now the foundation show is  happening on apple tv and though it's  not really been my cup of tea i haven't  seen the last few episodes i kind of  fell off i'm still happy that that has a  place and of course i'm really happy  about dune on the hyperion movie or tv  show that's getting made if you want to  learn more about interesting science  fiction lore check out my channel for  more videos all of my different series  are organized neatly into playlists  thanks guys  you
 

